58:%This paper presents significant generalizations of two results in rainbow graph theory, which originally required minimum degree conditions. We extend these results by weakening the hypotheses to Ore-type conditions. Specifically, we replace the minimum degree bounds with a more general Ore-type condition involving degree sums of non-adjacent vertices.. Let \( n \in \mathbb{N} \) with \( n \geq 3 \). Suppose \( \mathcal{G} = \{G_i: i\in [n]\) is a collection of \( n \)-graphs (not necessarily distinct) with the same vertex set \( V \). Define
