\begin{abstract}
Let $ n \in \mathbb{N} $ with $ n \geq 3 $, and let $\mathcal{G} = \{G_i:i\in [n]\} $ be a family of $ n $-vertex graphs on a common vertex set $V$, where the graphs in the family do not need to be distinct. A graph  $H$ with vertex set $V$ is  \emph{rainbow} in $\mathcal{G}$ if there exists an injection $ \phi: E(H) \to [n] $ such that $e \in E(G_{\phi(e)})$ for every edge $e \in E(H)$, where $|E(H)|\leq n$.  In 2020, Joos and Kim proved that $\mathcal{G}$ contains a rainbow Hamiltonian cycle under the Dirac-type condition. Recently, Liu, Chen, and Ma generalized this result by replacing the Dirac-type condition with a more general Ore-type condition involving degree sums of non-adjacent vertices: If $\sigma(\mathcal{G}) \geq n$, then $\mathcal{G}$ contains a rainbow Hamiltonian cycle, where the Ore-type condition $\sigma(\mathcal{G})$ is defined as follows:
$
\sigma(\mathcal{G}) = \min\{d_p(u) + d_q(v) \mid uv \notin E(G_i) \text{ for some } i \in [n] \text{ and for all } p, q \in [n]\}.
$
In this paper, under the Ore-type condition, we show that either each vertex of $V$ is contained in a rainbow cycle of length $\ell$ for every $\ell\in[4,n]$, or $G_1=\cdots=G_n=K_{\frac{n}{2},\frac{n}{2}}$. As a corollary, we deduce the rainbow pancyclicity of $\mathcal{G}$, which
 supports the famous meta-conjecture posed by Bondy. Furthermore, we prove rainbow vertex-pancyclicity of $\mathcal{G}$ under the Ore-type condition and provide an extremal graph family to show that the result is sharp.
%This paper presents significant generalizations of two results in rainbow graph theory, which originally required minimum degree conditions. We extend these results by weakening the hypotheses to Ore-type conditions. Specifically, we replace the minimum degree bounds with a more general Ore-type condition involving degree sums of non-adjacent vertices.. Let \( n \in \mathbb{N} \) with \( n \geq 3 \). Suppose \( \mathcal{G} = \{G_i: i\in [n]\) is a collection of \( n \)-graphs (not necessarily distinct) with the same vertex set \( V \). Define
%\[
%\sigma(\mathcal{G}) = \min\{d_p(u) + d_q(v) \mid uv \notin E(G_i) \text{ for some } i \in [n] \text{ and for all } p, q \in [n]\}.
%\] Our main contributions establish that if \( \sigma(\mathcal{G}) \geq n-1(n) \), then $\mathcal{G}$ possesses the desired rainbow cycle properties. These generalizations substantially broaden the applicability of the original theorems while maintaining their essential structural conclusions. We provide complete proofs for both generalizations and discuss the tightness of our conditions through constructive examples. The results contribute to the growing literature on transversal problems in graph theory and open new directions for research on degree-sum conditions in rainbow settings.
  


 \textbf{Keywords:} Graph families, Rainbow subgraphs, Ore-type condition, Pancyclicity
\end{abstract}

